course: dictionary
lesson: 6969
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Panda is a good example. «Red pandas live in cold mountain forests, wrap their thick tail around themselves like a blanket and have fur on the soles of their feet for icy branches.» The clues are cold mountain forests and icy branches, so this panda is the small animal, not the big bear.
explain: Clue words help you choose. «Protecting and joining up bamboo forests in China helped giant pandas.» The words giant and China point to the big black-and-white bear. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the clues around it? Then put your meaning back into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some meanings are old-fashioned, so you may not know them. In the UK, a «panda car» was a small police car. If you meet a word you know but it does not fit, stop and think about the clues, then check a dictionary to be sure.
fact: A giant panda is a large black-and-white bear from the mountain forests of China.
fact: Giant pandas eat almost only bamboo.
fact: A red panda is smaller, reddish-brown and furry, with a long ringed tail.
fact: Red pandas are not close relatives of giant pandas, even though both eat bamboo.
fact: In 2016, giant pandas moved from endangered to vulnerable, because wild numbers grew to about 1,800.
exercise: «Red pandas wrap their thick tail around themselves like a blanket.» Which panda is this sentence about? | *A small, reddish-brown animal with a long ringed tail | A bear with black-and-white fur | A kind of bamboo | A police car
exercise: «Protecting bamboo forests in China helped giant pandas.» Which clue tells you the panda is the bear? | A police car | Icy branches | A tail like a blanket | *Bamboo forests in China
exercise: In the UK, long ago, what was a «panda car»? | *A small police car | A reddish-brown animal | A soft toy | A large black-and-white bear
test: Which statement is true? | A giant panda has a long ringed tail | A giant panda is a small reddish-brown animal | A red panda is a close relative of the giant panda | *A red panda is smaller and reddish-brown, and is not a close relative of the giant panda
test: «Young pandas really tumble and roll, and pandas are good climbers.» What are pandas good at, according to the sentence? | Singing | Flying between trees | Swimming in rivers | *Climbing
exam: You read «The panda was parked outside the station» and are not sure which panda is meant. What should you do? | Pick the first meaning you remember without checking | Skip the sentence and never come back to it | *Use the clues around the word, try each meaning in the sentence, and check a dictionary if you are still unsure | Change the word to something you like better
